  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUPPORTING THE IMPLEMENTATION OF CAMEROON S (CITES) NATIONAL IVORY ACTION PLAN AND REDUCING THE SUPPLY OF IVORY FROM CAMEROON S TRIDOM REGION, THROUGH EFFECTIVE STOCKPILE MANAGEMENT.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT AN ELEPHANT CONSERVATION EFFORT IN CAMEROON BY STRENGTHENING THE IMPLEMENTATION OF THE NATIONAL IVORY ACTION PLAN (NIAP) AND IMPROVING LAW ENFORCEMENT CAPACITY. CAMEROON IS HOME TO APPROXIMATELY 6,830 ELEPHANTS. THIS PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE AFRICAN FOREST ELEPHANTS AND THEIR HABITAT BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OF POACHING AND IVORY TRAFFICKING. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) SUPPORTING THE CAMEROONIAN GOVERNMENT IN MAKING THEIR NIAP COMMITTEE FUNCTIONAL, INCLUDING CAPACITY DEVELOPMENT (2) DEVELOPING AND IMPLEMENTING AN IVORY STOCKPILE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM AND (3) BUILDING LAW ENFORCEMENT CAPACITY (INCLUDING THE MINISTRY OF FORESTS AND WILDLIFE) THROUGH TRAINING, INCLUDING THE MARKING, RECORDING AND MANAGEMENT OF SEIZED IVORY, LEGAL FRAMEWORKS, AND THE ELEPHANT TRADE INFORMATION SYSTEM (ETIS).</narrative>
  </description>
